3.3. Benzene-induced lamellocyte production and lymph gland dispersal is mediated by hematopoietic niche
The HSC/HPCs reside under the regulatory control of the stem cell microenvironment or niche. The niche commences progenitor differentiation in a non-autonomous way. Like vertebrates, Drosophila HSC/ HPCs maintenance is regulated by PSC (Drosophila hematopoietic niche). It has been well established that PSC plays a key role in mounting a proper immune response to infection and other stress conditions to maintain hematopoietic homeostasis [44]. To test whether PSC has any role in the benzene-induced hematopoietic emergency, we first analyzed benzene exposure's effect on PSC cell number and morphology. Antibody staining against Antennapedia (Antp), a PSC-specific biomarker, revealed no statistically significant changes \((P\!>\!0.05)\) in the PSC cell number or its morphology in all tested benzene concentrations compared to control (Fig. 3a–e). Further, we analyzed the non-autonomous function of the PSC in benzene-induced lamellocyte production and the lymph gland disruption. For that, the PSC was genetically ablated by target-specific overexpression of a pro-apoptotic gene, \(r p r\) , using a PSC-specific driver. A significant reduction in lamellocyte differentiation in \(10.0\,\mathrm{\mM}\) ( \(100\%\) , \(P\!<\!0.001]\) ) and \(100.0\,\mathrm{\mM}\) \((\sim\!95\%\) , \(P\!<\!0.001]\) ) benzene exposure after \(48\,\mathrm{h}\) was observed upon PSC ablation \((P c o l{>}G F P{>}r p r)\) , as compared to their respective genetic controls (Fig. 3f–j). Moreover, the PSC ablation \((P c o l{>}G F P{>}r p r)\) resulted in a significant reduction in the lymph gland dispersal of \(100\%\) and \(\sim\!92\%\) in \(10.0\,\mathrm{mM}\) \((P\!<\!0.005)\) and \(100.0\,\mathrm{mM}\) \((P\!<\!0.001)\) , respectively, after 96 h benzene exposure, compared to their respective genetic control, \(P c o l{>}G F P\) (Fig. 3k-o). Altogether, data suggest that PSC plays a critical role in activating immune response upon benzene exposure.
3.4. PSC mediates lamellocyte production and lymph gland dispersal via Toll/NF- \(\mathbf{\nabla\cdotKB}\) pathway upon benzene exposure
